			<div class="content" id="post-content-4839291">
									

<p>Awesome, thank you for the quick reply!<br />
I think I can keep this an interesting SCP proper, given some nice hefty changes. How do these changes sound:</p>
<p>1. Yes, on reflection I think there's no reason the Serpent's Hand needs to get involved (maybe they'll take an interest in a tale or somethin, or that interaction will just stay in my own headcanon).</p>
<p>2. However, I think the Chaos Insurgency still fits pretty well, and &quot;Coyote&quot; would definitely gravitate to them over the Foundation. But perhaps this turn of events works best as the final note?</p>
<p>3. Time to simplify the plot. Remove SH involvement, and go into less detail about the anthropologist character and how the Foundation discovered the SCP.</p>
<p>4. However, I'm not sure whether to remove the Foundation's attempted first contact (If I do keep it, I think I can rework it to make their method more interesting). If I keep it, it can open the storytelling opportunity for the next &quot;file&quot; to be a report of Coyote's betrayal and realignment with the CI. But of course, just cutting all that out would majorly simplify things.</p>
<p>Basically, I'm not sure whether it's acceptable for the most recent development to be Coyote &quot;joining&quot; the CI (and therefore being currently uncontained). Or perhaps the Foundation just throws resources at it via cultural suppression and weaken him so much that he stops being a problem (or so they think). That second ending might warrant an Ethics Committee log.</p>
<p>How do those changes and proposals sound?<br />
Thank you, I really appreciate the feedback, I do want to make a good article.</p>

